      en: "Tripoli sits in the heart of the Arcadian plateau and serves as a traditional center of the Peloponnese. The city combines administrative importance with a mountainous hinterland and a strong freedom-fighter legacy. Parks, squares, and a calm downtown shape its image, along with nearby historic battle sites. Tripoli is a useful stop between Nafplio, Sparta, and central Peloponnese destinations."
